  "id": "single-session-therapy",
  "term": "single-session therapy",
  "definition": "Single-session therapy is a way of delivering mental health care in which an evidence-based, solution-focused brief intervention is provided in one stand-alone therapy meeting. It can offer immediate psychological support and referrals, including while people are waiting for longer-term services.",
